  "details": "Currently, when using Test Build avatars or enabling debug features such as Avatar Debug, the effects are only visible locally. As a result, it is difficult for both the user and others to know whether these debug modes are active during use.\n\nTo improve clarity and transparency, I would like to request the following:\n\nWhen Avatar Debug or similar developer/debug tools are active, please add a visible icon or indicator (such as the earmuff icon) on the user's nameplate or avatar to signal to others that the avatar is currently in a debug/testing state.\n\nThis visual indicator should also apply when enabling other debug-related features such as eye raycasts, PB or contact, or any tool that would not normally be active in a standard experience.\n\nThis would help users:\n\nConfirm whether their own avatar is in a debug/test state\n\nClearly identify when someone else is using option that may affect how avatars or interactions behave\n\nIt would also help avoid misunderstandings or confusion during testing sessions, especially in shared or public worlds.",
